{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Maintain the Medical Cannabis Registry & Implement ACMD Recommendations of 2020",
        "additional_details": "The ACMD recommended that the Government continue a national CBPM patient registry & consider how private data could be captured. The Government accepted this.\r\n \r\nYet an NHS England response to an FoI request has confirmed that the registry, established in 2021, to inform NHS prescribing, has no patient entries, so no private data has been collected either.\r\n \r\nThe Government & the NHS have so far squandered the chance to build on valuable evidence on treatment effectiveness, patient outcomes & medication safety which should have been entered in this registry while patients are often still being told there is insufficient evidence for prescribing on the NHS.",
        "background": "We call upon the Government to safeguard & implement the NHS medical cannabis patient registry, to ensure that valuable prescribing data, treatment effectiveness, patient outcomes and adverse effects are collected from private medical cannabis clinics, where the vast majority of CBPMs are issued.",
